      "tokensOut": 14467,
      "answer": "JBrowse now shows HG002 nanopore reads over the SNRPN CpG island (chr15:24,953,500–24,957,500, hg38), coloured by 5mC and grouped by haplotype. I checked it in a screenshot, but the window was hidden, so that frame may be stale. HP 1 reads are mostly methylated (red) across the island and HP 2 reads mostly unmethylated (blue), which is the expected imprinted split. A third group, HP: none, holds the untagged reads.\n\nI couldn't use a published haplotagged file, so the HP tags are mine.\n- **ONT haplotagged CRAM:** its index is corrupt, and samtools fails on it too.\n- **Older ONT modBAM (`gm24385_mod_2021.09/extra_analysis/all.bam`):** it has no HP tag.\n- **My workaround:** I pulled reads for chr15:24.90–25.01 Mb from `all.bam` and haplotagged them against the phased SNPs in ONT's `wf_snp.vcf.gz`. I assigned HP by majority vote of each read's alleles at phased heterozygous SNPs. That gave 252 reads in HP 1, 207 in HP 2 and 68 untagged.\n\nThe local slice is `/tmp/jbrowse-agent-eval-cwd-nK4VH3/hg002_snrpn.tagged.bam`, and the track will stop loading if that file is removed. I also set `forceLoad` on the display, because the long reads otherwise trip the \"too much data\" gate."
    },
