      "answer": "I couldn't reproduce the haplotype split, because I couldn't find an HG002 nanopore modBAM to load. The hg38 config I opened has no methylation or nanopore alignment track. Four guessed jbrowse.org and S3 URLs for the BAM returned 404 or 403, and the bundled docs don't give a data URL. I didn't want to point the display at a made-up file, so nothing is set up. If you give me the BAM URL or a local path, I'll add it, set `baseColor` to modifications and group reads by their `HP` tag over the SNRPN CpG island."
